The local adaptation uses modern GT item capabilities and IGTTool classification,
preserving the source request bounds, simulated input queries and int addition.
It is an energy-phase adapter, not an IC2 or complete crafting implementation.
Modified source and build tools are available in the migration repository above;
locks/legacy-crafting-energy-source.json records the exact source expressions.

LegacyCraftingNbt.java ports the keeping-NBT phases of the same fixed GT5
GTShapedRecipe under LGPL-3.0. The source comparison expressions retain this
licence. LegacyItemTag.java is an original local binary adapter under MIT.
The comparison loads NBT classes from the official Minecraft 1.7.10 server
in an isolated class loader; that third-party binary is not redistributed.

